The complete fixed merged 1.patch (BakaSU manual hooks + lz4k + fixed execve) is generated by:

  python3 generate_1patch.py

This produces 1.patch (~39909 bytes) with:
  - ksu_handle_post_execveat on success and out_ret paths
  - pre-hook after local variable declarations (C89-safe)
  - CONFIG_KSU_MANUAL_HOOK for reboot
  - all original content (lz4k, path_umount, SELinux exports, other hooks)

One-liner from repo root:
  curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mingmingzhichu/build/main/generate_1patch.py | python3

Then: git apply 1.patch
